e is inked black  The overlying skin ellipse contains nipple areolar complex and measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The nipple is mobile and measures 1 4cm in greatest dimension  On sectioning  the breast parenchyma of the upper quadrants show an irregularly outlined gray white to tan pink  firm to hard mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The mass is located approximately between 11 and 1 o clock positions and is 0 8cm from the anterior surface and 7 0cm from the nearest posterior surface  Approximately 1 5cm posterior and lateral to this tumor  the breast parenchyma of the upper outer quadrant shows another irregularly outlined  tan pink to gray white  firm to hard possible tumor  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  This mass is located 1 8cm from the anterior surface and 6 0cm from the nearest posterior surface  The breast parenchyma surrounding both the tumors shows diffuse and dense fibrosis  In the remaining area  the breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense pink white fibrous stroma which is nodular focally and contains a few blue domed cysts measuring from 0 3cm up to 0 7cm in greatest dimension  Obvious lymph nodes are not identified in the lateral portion of the breast tissue  Sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger tumor  upper quadrants   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller possible tumor  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma between the 2 tumors   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from the tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral portion of the breast without lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm right simple mastectomy with a short stitch marking superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral end  The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  The overlying tan pink skin contains nipple areola complex and measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  The nipple is mobile and measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension  On sectioning  the breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink white fibrous stroma which is dense and nodular focally and contains a few blue domed cysts measuring from REMOVED_DATE up to 0 7cm in greatest dimension  An obvious tumor is not appreciated  On careful dissection  and on further evaluation  by specimen radiograph   one metallic clip and areas of microcalcifications are identified which are located in the upper outer quadrant  Obvious lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast tissue adjacent to the clip  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma adjacent to the clip with calcifications   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma adjacent to the areas of calcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Random sections of the breast away from the area of clips and microcalcifications  Received in formalin  and labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  On dissection  several tan pink to tan gray lymph nodes are identified measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The larger lymph nodes are bisected or serially sectioned  All the lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fourth largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next 4 larger lymph nodes  each bisected and 2 lymph nodes submitted in each cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining smaller lymph nodes  submitted in toto  Received in formalin  and labeled  right breast skin   is a disrupted fragment of tan pink skin with central defect  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm x up to 1 8cm  The specimen is not oriented  The skin surface is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is serially sectioned  Underlying breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast skin   are 3 fragments of unoriented skin with underlying fibrofatty breast tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm x up to 5cm  All the fragments are serially sectioned  The skin surface and the fibrofatty breast tissue are grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1A   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Friday February 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 24 47PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  invasive ductal carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  invasive lobular carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and pro