ectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm left simple mastectomy specimen with attached anterior skin and nipple  The specimen has been oriented with a short stitch superiorly and a long stitch lateral  The skin surface is remarkable for the presence of a 7 0cm firm linear incision which lies 13 5cm from the lateral  15 0cm from the medial  6 0cm from the superior  and 8 0cm from the inferior cutaneous margins  as well as 3 0cm to the superior and lateral of the nipple  Palpation reveals mild diffuse increased firmness and traction in the breast tissue underlying the scar  The posterior deep surgical margin consists of unremarkable yellow lobulated fibrofatty breast tissue and thin fascia with diffuse mild increased firmness centrally and in the superior lateral quadrant  The margins are inked black posteriorly and blue anteriorly  Serially sectioning through the posterior surface reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm cavity with smooth tan yellow walls and firm yellow nodules in the surrounding breast tissue  The cavity lies directly deep to the previously described incision  2 3cm deep to the skin surface  5 0cm from the deep margin  6 5cm from the inferior margin  13 0cm from the superior margin  16 0cm from the left lateral margin  18 0cm from the medial margin  An area of blue tracer dye is seen in the breast tissue abutting the skin surface and 15 0cm from the medial  20 0cm from the left lateral  10 5cm from the superior  and 10 0cm from the inferior margin  The remaining breast tissue is primarily fatty with no focal lesions identified  The superior lateral quadrant tissue is carefully examined for the presence of lymph nodes and none are felt  A separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue is received in the same container and is examined carefully  No gross lesions or lymph nodes are detected  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of sectioned cavity and adjacent breast tissue   REMOVED_